</ref> These include multiple {{MobSprite|Undead (Watcher);Undead}}s, as well as various {{miniboss}} mobs in higher floors. These mobs first appear as heads in display cases on the walls, which the Watcher flies to when picking to spawn.

The Watcher cannot be damaged, and trying to do so will cause him to attack back with a laser. In [[The Catacombs - Floor IV|Floor IV]] and above, he also has {{MobSprite|Watchful Eye|nolink=yes}}s to prevent players from going more than several blocks up in the arena.

Players who are dead when the fight starts or die during the fight are reanimated as a hostile {{MobSprite|Wandering Soul}} that resembles the player who died. Killing a Wandering Soul will revive the player it resembles. 

Once all of [[#Summoned Mobs|Mobs]] are summoned and killed, in the [[The Catacombs - Entrance|Entrance]] floor, the run completes. In all other floors, a portal will open to the main {{boss}} of that floor, and 1-2 {{Item|Dungeon Blessing|text=Blessings of Time V}} and a {{Item|Dungeon Blessing|text=Blessing of Power V}} will spawn. There is also a {{Chance|1.23%|1|81.3|rolls}} chance for an {{Item|Optical Lens}} to drop.

